a I, Rasche V, Kassubek J, M&#xfc;ller HP (2025) Hypothalamus and intracranial volume segmentation at the group level by use of a Gradio-CNN framework. Int J Comput Assist Radiol Surg 20:1723&#x2013;1731. https://doi.org/10.1007/s11548-025-03438-6</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1007/s11548-025-03438-6</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">40478471</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">12350493</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Gorges M, Kuntz B, Del Tredici K, Schmidt DG, M&#xfc;ller HP, Ludolph AC, Dupuis L, Kassubek J (2019) Morphological MRI investigations of the hypothalamus in 232 individuals with Parkinson&#x2019;s disease. Mov Disord 34:1566&#x2013;1570. https://doi.org/10.1002/mds.27814</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1002/mds.27814</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">31433875</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Kovacs GG, Lukic MJ, Irwin DJ, Arzberger T, Respondek G, Lee EB, Coughlin D, Giese A, Grossman M, Kurz C, McMillan CT, Gelpi E, Compta Y, van Swieten JC, Laat LD, Troakes C, Al-Sarraj S, Robinson JL, Roeber S, Xie SX, Lee VM, Trojanowski JQ, H&#xf6;glinger GU (2020) Distribution patterns of tau pathology in progressive supranuclear palsy. Acta Neuropathol 140:99&#x2013;119. https://doi.org/10.1007/s00401-020-02158-2</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1007/s00401-020-02158-2</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">32383020</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">7360645</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>H&#xf6;glinger GU, Sch&#xf6;pe J, Stamelou M, Kassubek J, Del Ser T, Boxer AL, Wagenpfeil S, Huppertz HJ, AL-108-231 Investigators; Tauros MRI Investigators; Movement Disorder Society-Endorsed PSP Study Group (2017) Longitudinal magnetic resonance imaging in progressive supranuclear palsy: a new combined score for clinical trials. Mov Disord 32:842&#x2013;852. https://doi.org/10.1002/mds.26973</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId